compile-file of cl-ppcre/lexer.lisp SEGFAULTS (the compiled load path)
=====================================================================

STATUS
------
INTERPRETED cl-ppcre now works completely (bug-cl-ppcre cascade fixed through
v1.9.6): loading the sources with LOAD and calling SCAN / REGEX-REPLACE-ALL /
ALL-MATCHES-AS-STRINGS / SPLIT all give correct results.  But the ORIGINAL
ticket's path — (ql:quickload :cl-ppcre), which COMPILE-FILEs each source —
SIGSEGVs.

REPRO
-----
    (dolist (f '("packages" "specials" "util" "errors" "charset" "charmap"
                 "chartest" "lexer" ...))
      (compile-file <cl-ppcre>/f.lisp :output-file ...) (load ...))
crashes (exit 139) while COMPILING lexer.lisp.  packages…chartest compile+load
fine; lexer is the first to crash.

NARROWING SO FAR
----------------
* Interpreted LOAD of lexer.lisp: OK.
* (compile nil `(lambda () ,form)) for each top-level form of lexer.lisp: does
  NOT segfault.
So the crash is specific to COMPILE-FILE (the VM compiler + cfasl writer path,
or a GC during the larger compile-file operation), not to plain COMPILE or to
interpretation.  Next step: run under gdb (BOCL_GCSTRESS / a debug build) to
catch the faulting form/frame in COMPILE-FILE on lexer.lisp; suspect the cfasl
externaliser or a rooting gap on the compile-file path.

This is the remaining blocker for bug-cl-ppcre's compiled (quicklisp) path;
the interpreter side is done.  Discovered 2026-07-24.
